#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg.rst:5
msgid "Common Primary Timing Generator (CMTG)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:21
msgid ""
"The CMTG is a timing generator that runs in parallel to transcoders timing "
"generators (TG) to provide a synchronization mechanism where CMTG acts as "
"primary and transcoders TGs act as secondary to the CMTG. The CMTG outputs "
"its TG start and frame sync signals to the transcoders that are configured "
"as secondary, which use those signals to synchronize their own timing with "
"the CMTG's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:28
msgid ""
"The CMTG can be used only with eDP or MIPI command mode and supports the "
"following use cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:31
msgid ""
"Dual eDP: The CMTG can be used to keep two eDP TGs in sync when on a dual "
"eDP configuration (with or without PSR/PSR2 enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:34
msgid ""
"Single eDP as secondary: It is also possible to use a single eDP "
"configuration with the transcoder TG as secondary to the CMTG. That would "
"allow a flow that would not require a modeset on the existing eDP when a new "
"eDP is added for a dual eDP configuration with CMTG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:39
msgid ""
"DC6v: In DC6v, the transcoder might be off but the CMTG keeps running to "
"maintain frame timings. When exiting DC6v, the transcoder TG then is synced "
"back the CMTG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/cmtg:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cmtg.c:43
msgid ""
"Currently, the driver does not use the CMTG, but we need to make sure that "
"we disable it in case we inherit a display configuration with it enabled."
msgstr ""
